From: qyYue1389 <qyYue1389@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Wed, 16 Sep 2026 08:32:33 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 19/19] feat(rl): log the beta decomposition of the flow gap

z_t is an arithmetic group mean, so Eq. 6 splits exactly and g is linear in
beta:

    g_i = [mean_group(beta*r) - beta*r_i] + [mean_group(d) - d_i]

Two readings of a training log depend on that split and were not measurable
before:

  * On a reward-degenerate group the reward term is identically zero, so g is
    pure drift. The gradient there is flow matching toward pi_ref*exp(beta*r)/Z,
    not reward learning. 67-70 percent of groups on this dataset are degenerate,
    so that is the majority of every batch -- worth stating precisely rather
    than claiming the arm keeps learning reward where GRPO gives zero.
  * Lowering beta does not cure clip saturation. It shrinks only the reward half
    and leaves drift untouched, so what survives the clip gets MORE
    drift-dominated. beta has to be picked on reward_term/drift_term, not on
    clip_saturation alone.

New metrics: reward_term_abs_mean, drift_term_abs_mean, nondegenerate_frac,
sign_agree_nondegenerate, sat_at_beta_2/4/8/16. The sweep reuses the same r and
d, so it costs no forward pass; the whole block is elementwise on tensors
already in hand, in a function whose share of a 920s step was 0.09s.

sat_at_beta_<configured beta> must equal clip_saturation. That identity is the
block's own self-check and is now asserted in p7_fixedpoint_check.py, together
with the split identity and the degenerate-group count. Measured there:
0.000e+00, 1.192e-07, 0.7500. Fixed point unchanged at 7.389644e-13.

---
 verl/trainer/ppo/ray_trainer.py | 45 +++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++
 1 file changed, 45 insertions(+)

diff --git a/verl/trainer/ppo/ray_trainer.py b/verl/trainer/ppo/ray_trainer.py
index c1523258..4df359c2 100644
--- a/verl/trainer/ppo/ray_trainer.py
+++ b/verl/trainer/ppo/ray_trainer.py
@@ -356,6 +356,51 @@ def compute_gflowrl_flow_gap(
         "gflowrl/clip_saturation": float(saturated),
         "gflowrl/y_len_mean": float(L.mean()),
     }
+
+    # ---- diagnostics.  No gradient, no effect on what this function returns. ----
+    # z_t is an ARITHMETIC group mean, so Eq. 6 splits exactly into two additive
+    # halves and g is linear in beta:
+    #
+    #     g_i = [mean_group(beta*r) - beta*r_i] + [mean_group(d) - d_i]
+    #            reward term, proportional to beta   drift term, independent of beta
+    #
+    # Two things follow that are easy to misread from a training log:
+    #
+    #   * On a reward-degenerate group the reward term is identically zero, so g is
+    #     pure drift.  The gradient there is flow matching toward pi_ref*exp(beta*r)/Z,
+    #     NOT reward learning -- do not report it as the latter.  On this dataset
+    #     67-70% of groups are degenerate, so this is the majority of the batch.
+    #   * Lowering beta does not cure clip saturation.  It shrinks only the reward
+    #     half and leaves drift untouched, so what survives the clip becomes MORE
+    #     drift-dominated.  Choose beta on reward_term/drift_term, not on
+    #     clip_saturation alone.
+    #
+    # The beta sweep reuses the same r and d, so it costs no forward pass and no
+    # extra memory.  sat_at_beta_<beta> must come out equal to clip_saturation --
+    # that identity is this block's own self-check, visible in every logged step.
+
+    def _group_mean(x):
+        s = torch.zeros(n_groups, dtype=torch.float32, device=x.device)
+        s = s.index_add_(0, gidx, x.float())
+        return (s / cnts.clamp(min=1.0))[gidx]
+
+    reward_term = _group_mean(beta * r) - beta * r
+    drift_term = g - reward_term            # exact by construction, every variant
+    nondeg = reward_term.abs() > 1e-12
+    metrics["gflowrl/reward_term_abs_mean"] = float(reward_term.abs().mean())
+    metrics["gflowrl/drift_term_abs_mean"] = float(drift_term.abs().mean())
+    metrics["gflowrl/nondegenerate_frac"] = float(nondeg.float().mean())
+    if bool(nondeg.any()):
+        # does the clip still preserve the reward ordering where reward exists?
+        metrics["gflowrl/sign_agree_nondegenerate"] = float(
+            (torch.sign(g[nondeg]) == torch.sign(reward_term[nondeg])).float().mean()
+        )
+    for _b in (2.0, 4.0, 8.0, 16.0):
+        _g = _group_mean(_b * r + d_in_z) - d_in_g - _b * r
+        metrics[f"gflowrl/sat_at_beta_{_b:g}"] = float(
+            ((_g < -eps_low) | (_g > eps_high)).float().mean()
+        )
+
     return data, metrics
 
 
